    {
      "id": "white",
      "name": "Fawn",
      "description": "A darkened topline in the manner of sooty - a soft band down the crest, back and croup with no edge to it at either end - and, sitting on that dark band and nowhere else, one consecutive run of small round spots somewhere between the neck and the rump. Never two clusters with a gap between them, never a spiral or a pattern, just a flowing line of them, and all of them small. They keep off the face, the belly and the legs. Most fawn horses also carry a stylised eyeliner, a pangare-like lightening underneath, and a pale underside to the tail.",
